diff --git a/features/filters.feature b/features/filters.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..863f52f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filters.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Feature: Filtering and routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on what is active or completed
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And I have todos "Buy milk", "Walk dog", "Read book"
+    And "Buy milk" is completed
+    And "Walk dog" is completed
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    When I navigate to "#/"
+    Then I see 3 todos in the list
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the todo label reads "Read book"
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo while in active filter hides it
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I complete "Read book"
+    Then I see 0 todos in the list
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    Then I see 2 todos in the list
+    And the todos are "Buy milk" and "Walk dog"
+
+  Scenario: Un-completing a todo while in completed filter hides it
+    When I navigate to "#/completed"
+    And I un-complete "Buy milk"
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the todo label reads "Walk dog"
+
+  Rule: Filter link selection
+
+  Scenario: The selected filter link has class "selected"
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "All" does not have class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "Completed" does not have class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Navigating back to all filter shows filter state
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And I navigate to "#/"
+    Then the filter link for "All" has class "selected"
+    And the filter link for "Active" does not have class "selected"
