+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page loads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Save and restore
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist in localStorage after being created
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I type "Walk dog" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then localStorage has 2 items stored under key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Scenario: Reloading restores todos from localStorage
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk" stored in localStorage
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then I see 1 todo in the list
+    And the todo label reads "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists across reloads
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk" stored in localStorage
+    And "Buy milk" is marked completed in localStorage
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: The active filter is persisted on reload
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk" stored in localStorage
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the filter link for "Active" has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: LocalStorage keys use id, title, completed fields
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    Then localStorage items for "todos-vanillajs" have "id", "title", and "completed" fields
